	<entry>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  delete in select]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=15371#p15371"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Bon, j&#039;ai trouvé une solution élégante sur le net <a href="http://www.postgresonline.com/journal/archives/22-Deleting-Duplicate-Records-in-a-Table.html" rel="nofollow">http://www.postgresonline.com/journal/a … Table.html</a> &quot;DELETING DUPLICATE RECORDS IN A TABLE&quot; :</p><div class="codebox"><pre><code>yt_tests=# select ctid, * from cities where cities.name like &#039;Merr%&#039; ;
 ctid  |  name  | location 
-------+--------+----------
 (0,2) | Merris | (0.5,49)
 (0,4) | Merris | (0.5,49)
(2 rows)

yt_tests=# select max(ctid) from cities where cities.name like &#039;Merr%&#039; ;
  max  
-------
 (0,4)
(1 row)

yt_tests=# delete from cities where ctid not in (select max(ctid) from cities where cities.name like &#039;Merr%&#039;);
DELETE 1

yt_tests=# select ctid, * from cities where cities.name like &#039;Merr%&#039; ;
 ctid  |  name  | location 
-------+--------+----------
 (0,4) | Merris | (0.5,49)
(1 row)</code></pre></div><p>Toute l&#039;astuce est de prendre le max de ctid...</p>]]></content>
